<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment ABOVE the root breaks
        `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading parent-xml error.

        Description reworded 2026-08-31 (Acquisitions gap-fix, Item 6.2/6.4,
        design-requirements.md §1/§2 ITEM 6) to state the field's POPULATION explicitly. See
        Deals_Lost__c.field-meta.xml (this folder) for the full metric-inversion reasoning this
        wording protects against: this field, like its three siblings (Deals_Won__c,
        Deals_Lost__c, First_Submission_DateTime__c), counts only brokers who have a Contact.
        Type and maintenance mechanism are unchanged by this edit.
    -->
    <fullName>Deals_Submitted__c</fullName>
    <description>Count of this broker's Opportunities, any stage. Covers ONLY brokers who have a Contact (Lead converted) - see Deals_Lost__c for the full population caveat. Authoritative population: brokerLeaderboard / BrokerLeaderboardService. Maintained nightly by BrokerCounterRecalcBatch. Not a native roll-up (Leads are not master-detail children of Contact).</description>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <label>Deals Submitted</label>
    <precision>18</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
